; rungs/clips-skeleton.eval - a skeleton swinging at the party, the rung
; tools\CombatTest.py's CLIPS check sweeps (code-review C73).
;
; The check is about the monster's ATTACK clip: it adds a second one and demands
; the sweep's dice do not move. So this rung is the monster swinging, again and
; again - a skeleton stood up beside the party, which does not swing back (the
; novice rung's party kills its skeleton before it ever swings, so a second
; attack clip would never be picked there). Twelve seconds is about seven
; swings: every one rolls to hit and for damage, and every one starts an attack
; clip. A plain skeleton cannot down the whole party in that time.
;
; Like every rung it assumes nothing about what ran before and sets no seed:
; the sweep owns the seed.

heal
arena open 9 9
spawn skeleton 14 11 south 1 up
tp 14 12
face n
tally reset
step 12
tally
